## 🔑 Environment Variables Setup (.env)

### 📌 Backend `.env` (inside /backend)

PORT=5000
MONGO_URI=mongodb+srv://Door2Go:Door2Go123@door2go.opetk5r.mongodb.net/door2goDB?retryWrites=true&w=majority&appName=Door2Go
JWT_SECRET=your_secure_jwt_secret


✅ Used for:
- Database connection
- User authentication
- Token security

---

### 📌 Frontend `.env` (root directory)

VITE_API_URL=https://door2goo.onrender.com/api

✅ Used for:
- Connecting frontend to backend API

---

## 🔌 API Endpoints Overview

### 🔐 Authentication
- POST `/api/auth/register`
- POST `/api/auth/login`

### 👤 Users & Profiles
- GET `/api/users/profile`
- PUT `/api/users/profile`

### 🛒 Cart
- POST `/api/cart/add`
- GET `/api/cart`
- DELETE `/api/cart/remove/:id`

### ✅ Checkout
- POST `/api/checkout`

### 📦 Orders
- GET `/api/orders`
- PUT `/api/orders/:id/status`

### 🚚 Drivers
- GET `/api/driver/orders`
- PUT `/api/driver/pickup/:id`
- PUT `/api/driver/deliver/:id`

### 🛍 Products
- GET `/api/products`
- GET `/api/products/:id`

---

# 🔐 Phase 4 Documentation  
## Security, Roles & Backup

---

## ✅ 1. Security Implementation

### 🔑 Authentication System
- JWT-based authentication
- Secure password hashing using bcrypt
- Token generation handled in:
backend/utils/tokens.js



### 🛡 Route Protection
- Protected backend routes using:
backend/middleware/auth.js


- Only authenticated users can access:
- Cart
- Checkout
- Orders
- Profile

### ❗ Global Error Handling
- Centralized error handling in:
backend/middleware/error.js



---

## ✅ 2. Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)

### 🎭 Roles Implemented
- **Customer**
- **Driver**
- **Admin**

### ✅ Access Restrictions
- Customers:
- Can add to cart
- Can checkout
- Can track orders
- Drivers:
- Can only access Driver Console
- Pickup & deliver orders
- Admin:
- Full backend access

### 📂 Role Logic Stored In
backend/models/User.js


---

## ✅ 3. Data Protection

- Environment variables hidden using `.env`
- `.gitignore` prevents leaking secrets
- JWT secret protected
- Database credentials secured via environment variables

---

## ✅ 4. Backup Strategy

### 🗄 Database Backup (MongoDB Atlas)
- Automatic cloud backups enabled
- Point-in-time recovery
- Daily snapshot backups

### 💾 Code Backup
- GitHub repository stores:
  - All frontend
  - All backend
  - Deployment configs

### ☁ Platform Redundancy
- Frontend hosted on Vercel
- Backend hosted on Render
- Database on MongoDB Atlas
- Each layer fully independent

---

## 🚀 Deployment Setup

---

### ✅ Frontend Deployment (Vercel)

1. Push project to GitHub
2. Import project into Vercel
3. Set environment variable:
VITE_API_URL=https://door2goo.onrender.com/api


4. Deploy

✅ Frontend auto rebuilds on each push

---

### ✅ Backend Deployment (Render)

1. Create Web Service
2. Connect GitHub backend repo
3. Set Root Directory:
backend

4. Add environment variables:

PORT=5000
MONGO_URI=mongodb+srv://Door2Go:Door2Go123@door2go.opetk5r.mongodb.net/door2goDB?retryWrites=true&w=majority&appName=Door2Go
JWT_SECRET=your_secure_jwt_secret

5. Deploy

✅ Backend stays online 24/7

---

### ✅ Database Setup (MongoDB Atlas)

1. Create Free Cluster
2. Add Database User
3. Add Network Access `0.0.0.0/0`
4. Copy connection string
5. Paste into Render `.env`

